<title>ITALY: Italy's Trieste sees June CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Trieste sees June CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>TRIESTE, Italy 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Trieste said its June consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 0.9 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In May Trieste's inflation rate was 0.3 percent month-on-month and 1.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Trieste is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Friday and Monday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.49 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>The following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to May 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1    (0.3)    0.9    (1.1)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.1    (0.1)   -0.4    (0.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0    (0.4)    3.1    (3.1)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.0   (-0.2)    2.8    (2.9)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.1    (0.6)    2.3    (2.3)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.1    (0.0)    1.9    (1.8)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0    (0.2)   -2.6   (-2.5)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.1    (0.4)   -0.2   (-0.4)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.3    (0.0)    5.1    (4.8)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.3    (0.0)    2.4    (2.9)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0    (1.4)    0.6    (0.7)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129507</p>
